Under the opt-in `--modular-termination`, `dafny build --target:lib` records in the `.doo` library a termination record: hashes of its program, of the verifying build of Dafny and its prelude, of the Z3 binary and of its semantic options, and the termination contract of each module it defines and of each library module it was verified against. The record, itself covered by a hash, is written only when the whole program was conclusively verified without unchecked premises (`assume`, `{:axiom}`, bodyless members, `{:extern}`, `--allow-axioms`). Under the option, a module cannot refine or replace a library module. Under the option, a library is admitted only when its record matches its program, this build, the current solver and options, and the contracts of the libraries loaded with it; source libraries, `.dll` libraries and the bundled standard library are rejected. Without the option, libraries built with it are rejected and other libraries are read as before.
